<title>USA: General Growth Q1 FFO shr $0.64 vs $0.55.</title>
<headline>General Growth Q1 FFO shr $0.64 vs $0.55.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share data - Unaudited)</p>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31,</p>
<p>							   1997	   1996</p>
<p>FUNDS FROM OPERATIONS (FFO)</p>
<p>FFO -- Operating Partnership		  $31,119	$23,735</p>
<p>Less: Allocations to</p>
<p>Operating Partnership</p>
<p>	unitholders				 $11,410	 $8,810</p>
<p> FFO -- REIT stockholders		     $19,709	$14,925</p>
<p> FFO per share					$0.64	  $0.55</p>
<p>Average REIT shares assuming full</p>
<p> conversion of operating partnership units 48,913	 43,373</p>
<p>PORTFOLIO RESULTS (a)</p>
<p> Total revenues				   $97,869	$84,441</p>
<p> Operating expenses			    (44,651)     (35,515)</p>
<p> Net operating income			    53,218	 48,926</p>
<p>  Interest expense, net			(22,099)     (25,191)</p>
<p>    FFO -- operating Partnership	     31,119	 23,735</p>
<p>Depreciation and amortization --</p>
<p>	Real Estate				(15,605)     (15,405)</p>
<p>Straight line rent (not included in FFO, so</p>
<p>it must be added in order to reconcile to</p>
<p>	GAAP net income)			    1,355	  1,458</p>
<p>    Net gain on sales (c)			58,626	     --</p>
<p>Allocations to operating</p>
<p>	partnership unitholders		(27,542)	(2,792)</p>
<p>    Income before extraordinary item	 47,953	  6,996</p>
<p>Extraordinary item -- charges related to</p>
<p>	early retirement of debt		  (377)	(2,291)</p>
<p>    Net income				    $47,576	 $4,705</p>
<p> Average REIT shares			     30,978	 27,273</p>
<p> Per Share before extraordinary item	  $1.55	  $0.26</p>
<p>    Extraordinary item			   (0.01)	 (0.08)</p>
<p>    Net income per share			  $1.54	  $0.18</p>
<p>NOTES: (a) Portfolio results combine revenues and expenses of General Growth Management Inc and properties owned by Operating Partnership with 38.21% of the revenues and expenses of property interests owned by GGP/Homart and the Company's share (see note (b)) of revenues and expenses of property interests owned by CenterMark.</p>
<p>(b)  On January 2, 1997, the Company completed the sale of its interest in CenterMark.  Accordingly, the 1996 portfolio results reflect a 30% interest in CenterMark, and the 1997 results exclude CenterMark.</p>
<p>(c)  Includes gain on sale of remaining interest in CenterMark less additional costs related to prior acquisitions.</p>
<p>Full company name is General Growth Properties INc.</p>
